Linux compat for package:skyline widgets/yoga.dart.

1. YGConnector.updateChildren/removeChild call coordinateStackingChildren()
   unconditionally.  That method asserts enableStackingPaint; connectors created
   without stacking (the Linux runtime) therefore threw when the native side
   updated children.  Guard the call; non-stacking connectors paint via
   firstChild.
2. Native-view hit testing: plain YGNode render objects do not forward hit
   tests to their single child, so the texture widget's RenderPointerListener
   never saw pointers.  Treat kTexture like a proxy for hit testing (report the
   hit; hitTestWithPaintTransform adds the listener exactly once).
3. Connector-backed YGNodes: the shadow-node hit test is authoritative.  The raw
   RenderBox fallback (YGConnectorRenderObject.hitTest == size.contains) made
   every full-viewport fixed/portal overlay swallow all pointers, so scroll
   views behind it never received gestures (the address-book root-portal A-Z
   index blocked the whole page).

diff --git a/packages/skyline/lib/widgets/yoga.dart b/packages/skyline/lib/widgets/yoga.dart
index a4e132f..51fdb84 100644
--- a/packages/skyline/lib/widgets/yoga.dart
+++ b/packages/skyline/lib/widgets/yoga.dart
@@ -768,6 +768,15 @@ class YGNodeRenderObject extends YGRenderBox
         !enableLayoutParagraph && concreteWidgetType == WidgetType.kText) {
       return hitTestYGConnector(result, position);
     }
+    if (concreteWidgetType == WidgetType.kTexture) {
+      // Native views: report the hit without adding the listener here;
+      // hitTestWithPaintTransform adds it exactly once.
+      final RenderBox? textureChild = child;
+      return textureChild != null &&
+          textureChild.hasSize &&
+          textureChild.size.contains(position);
+    }
+
     if (concreteWidgetType == WidgetType.kHero) {
       return hitTestHero(result, position);
     }
@@ -798,7 +807,13 @@ class YGNodeRenderObject extends YGRenderBox
       return true;
     }
 
-    if (hitTestYGNode(result, position)) {
+    // Connector-backed nodes already ran the authoritative shadow-node hit
+    // test above.  YGConnectorRenderObject.hitTest only checks the whole box,
+    // so falling back to it would make a full-viewport fixed/portal overlay
+    // swallow pointers even when no child contains the point (blocking the
+    // scroll view behind the address-book A-Z index).
+    if (concreteWidgetType != WidgetType.kYGConnector &&
+        hitTestYGNode(result, position)) {
       result.add(BoxHitTestEntry(this, position));
       return true;
     }
@@ -905,7 +920,9 @@ class YGConnector extends SkylineMultiChildRenderObjectWidget
 
     // Proactively update stacking children in case it's paint method is not
     // being called somehow, which leads to memory leak and hitTest issue.
-    renderObject?.coordinateStackingChildren();
+    if (renderObject?.enableStackingPaint ?? false) {
+      renderObject?.coordinateStackingChildren();
+    }
     assert(!children.contains(child));
     markNeedsLayout();
   }
@@ -929,7 +946,11 @@ class YGConnector extends SkylineMultiChildRenderObjectWidget
 
     // Proactively update stacking children in case it's paint method is not
     // being called somehow, which leads to memory leak and hitTest issue.
-    renderObject?.coordinateStackingChildren();
+    // Linux compat: non-stacking connectors must not call this (it asserts
+    // enableStackingPaint); they paint via firstChild anyway.
+    if (renderObject?.enableStackingPaint ?? false) {
+      renderObject?.coordinateStackingChildren();
+    }
     markNeedsLayout();
   }
 
